🐘 Database

Diamond Pi Coin uses PostgreSQL as its primary relational database.

Core Tables

users
assets
wallets
transactions

Users

Stores account information and authentication-related identifiers.

Assets

Stores supported digital assets, symbols, names, types, and pricing data.

Wallets

Stores user balances, locked balances, asset relationships, and deposit addresses.

Transactions

Stores:

- Deposit
- Withdrawal
- Transfer
- Send
- Receive
- Swap
- Amount
- Fee
- Status
- Reference
- Transaction hash

The database architecture uses high-precision numeric fields suitable for digital-asset accounting.

